# Banking Analytics – Dataset Documentation

A collection of synthetic banking datasets used to build the **Enterprise Banking – Credit Risk & Portfolio Intelligence Platform** using Microsoft Power BI.

The datasets simulate a banking environment and support loan portfolio analysis, credit risk monitoring, customer analytics, branch performance, and collections analysis.

All data is fictional and created exclusively for portfolio demonstration. No confidential customer or employer data is used.

---

## 1. Source Datasets

The project consists of six CSV datasets.

| Dataset | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `Dim_Branch` | Dimension | Branch details, locations, regions, managers and annual targets |
| `Dim_Customer` | Dimension | Customer demographics, income, employment and branch mapping |
| `Dim_Product` | Dimension | Loan products, interest rates and maximum tenure |
| `Fact_Loan` | Fact | Loan details, disbursements, outstanding balances and delinquency |
| `Fact_Payment` | Fact | Payment schedules, due amounts, paid amounts and payment status |
| `Fact_Collections` | Fact | Collection assignments, overdue amounts and recovery details |

## 2. Supporting Power BI Tables

The following tables are created within the Power BI model and are not separate source datasets.

| Table | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `Dim_Calendar` | Date-based analysis and reporting |
| `Portfolio_Performance` | Performing and Non-Performing portfolio classification |
| `Customer_Risk_Segment` | Customer risk segmentation |
| `SecurityAccess` | User access mapping for Dynamic Row-Level Security |

## 3. Analytical Coverage

The datasets support analysis across the following business areas:

- Loan portfolio and outstanding exposure
- Credit risk, NPA and delinquency
- Customer demographics and risk segmentation
- Loan product performance
- Branch and regional performance
- Collections and recovery efficiency
- Payment behaviour and trends

## 4. Data Model

The datasets are integrated into a dimensional model in Power BI.

The model consists of three fact tables, three core dimension tables, and supporting tables for date analysis, portfolio classification, customer segmentation and security.

It supports interactive reporting, DAX calculations, cross-dimensional analysis and Dynamic Row-Level Security.

For more details, see the [Data Model Documentation](../03_Data_Model/README.md).

## 5. Data Privacy

- All datasets contain synthetic records.
- Customer details, identifiers, email addresses and financial values are fictional.
- Security access records are for demonstration purposes only.
- No confidential employer or production banking data is included.
- The editable Power BI project file is maintained separately.

## 6. Disclaimer

This is an independently developed portfolio project. It does not represent an actual bank, financial institution or production banking system. All data is intended solely for educational and demonstration purposes.
